---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AdSlot from '../components/AdSlot.astro';
import { currentMonthYear } from '../utils/site-date';
import AppealLetter from '../components/AppealLetter.astro';
import AirportSidebar from '../components/AirportSidebar.astro';

const title = "Appeal Your Birmingham Airport Drop-Off Charge | Free PCN Appeal Letter 2026";
const description = "Received a parking charge notice for dropping off at Birmingham Airport? Use our free appeal letter template and beat your PCN in minutes.";
const canonical = "https://appealairportpcn.co.uk/birmingham-drop-off-charge-appeal/";

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "How to Appeal a Birmingham Airport Drop-Off Charge",
  "description": "Step-by-step guide and free appeal letter template for challenging a Birmingham Airport drop-off PCN.",
  "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "AppealPCN" },
  "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "AppealAirportPCN.co.uk" },
};

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much is the Birmingham drop-off charge?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The Drop Off car park is free for up to 10 minutes. It costs £7 for 10 to 15 minutes. The Premium Set Down area has a separate tariff and currently costs £8 for the first 15 minutes." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I appeal a Birmingham drop-off charge?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Appeal to the operator using the instructions on your PCN. If your appeal is rejected, check whether the notice gives you a POPLA code." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "I was only there for a few minutes, do I still have to pay?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "It depends on which area you used and which entry and exit times were recorded. Check the ANPR photos and the location shown by the airport before deciding what to do." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is the charge a council fine?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "No. This is a private parking charge. It is not a council fine." }
    },
  ],
};

const tips = [
  { heading: 'Act within 28 days', body: 'The deadline to appeal is 28 days from the notice date. Miss it and you lose the right to formally appeal.' },
  { heading: 'Use recorded post', body: "If sending by post, always use Royal Mail Tracked or Signed For. Keep your proof of postage." },
  { heading: 'Request the evidence', body: 'Ask for the ANPR photographs in your appeal. Operators must provide them, and they sometimes reveal errors.' },
  { heading: 'POPLA is free', body: "If rejected, you can escalate to POPLA at no cost. Do not pay before exhausting this option." },
  { heading: 'Keep a copy', body: "Save or print a copy of everything you send. You'll need it if the case escalates." },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  currentPage="birmingham"
  schema={[articleSchema, faqSchema]}
>

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumb">
        <div class="wrap"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><a href="/birmingham-drop-off-charge-appeal/">Birmingham</a></div>
      </nav>
      <h1>Appeal Your Birmingham Airport Drop-Off Charge</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">Received an unexpected parking charge notice after dropping someone off at Birmingham? You may well have grounds to challenge it, and our free template makes the process straightforward.</p>
  </section>

  <main>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="main-content">
        <div class="content-grid">

          <AirportSidebar current="Birmingham Airport" tips={tips} />

          <div class="airport-main-column">
            <AppealLetter airport="Birmingham Airport">
              <p>I appeal as the registered keeper of the vehicle. I am not obliged to identify the driver and decline to do so.</p>
              <p>1. The parking operator cannot hold the registered keeper liable for this charge. The drop-off zone at Birmingham Airport is on land under statutory control, including the Birmingham Airport Byelaws 2021 made under sections 63 and 64 of the Airports Act 1986. The land is therefore not "relevant land" under paragraph 3(1)(c) of Schedule 4 to the Protection of Freedoms Act 2012 ("POFA"). The POFA keeper liability provisions do not apply, and the operator has no lawful basis to pursue the registered keeper.</p>
              <p>2. This charge is not a byelaw penalty. It is a contractual parking charge, which can only be claimed from the driver. If the airport wished to enforce against keepers under its byelaws, that would be a matter for the airport. The operator does not own the airport and has not said it acts under the byelaws. The Single Code of Practice (section 3.1.3, Note 2) says operators must not confuse the enforcement of byelaws with the contractual application of parking charges.</p>
              <p>3. The charge was not brought to the driver's attention before the contract was formed. Under Thornton v Shoe Lane Parking [1971] 2 QB 163, terms that are not brought to the other party's attention before the contract is made do not bind them. The operator must show that the charge was clearly displayed before the vehicle entered the zone.</p>
              <p>4. The signage does not comply with section 3 of the Private Parking Sector Single Code of Practice. In particular:<br>
                - There was no entrance sign showing that terms apply and whether payment is required (3.1.1 and 3.1.2).<br>
                - The charge was not shown in a large, legible font (3.1.3(j) and 3.1.4).<br>
                - The signs could not be read on approach or in the lighting conditions (3.1.3(b) and 3.1.6).<br>
              Without clear terms shown before the driver committed to entering the zone, no valid contractual offer was made. The operator is put to strict proof, with dated photographs, of the signs in place at the time.</p>
              <p>The registered keeper cannot be presumed or inferred to have been the driver, nor pursued under any interpretation of agency law. The Notice to Keeper can only hold the driver liable. Any reliance on Elliott v Loake would not assist: that was a criminal case decided on forensic and other evidence, not a presumption that the keeper was driving. The operator has produced no evidence of who was driving.</p>
              <p>I require this PCN to be cancelled and ask for written confirmation.</p>
            </AppealLetter>

            <div class="instructions-card">
              <h2>How to use this appeal template</h2>
              <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">1</div><div class="step-text">Click <strong>"Copy template"</strong> above, the full appeal is copied to your clipboard.</div></div>
              <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">2</div><div class="step-text">Log into the operator's online appeal system (or open your PCN) and paste the template into the appeal text box.</div></div>
              <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">3</div><div class="step-text">Submit and wait for a decision. The operator must respond within 35 days.</div></div>
              <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">4</div><div class="step-text">If rejected, request your POPLA code and escalate to the free, independent adjudicator, operators lose the vast majority of cases on these grounds.</div></div>
            </div>

            <div class="airport-info-panel">
            <section class="intro-section">
              <h2>Birmingham drop-off charge appeal</h2>
              <p>Got a PCN for dropping someone off at Birmingham? It's highly likely you can cancel it. Use the free template above.</p>

              <h3>The charge</h3>
              <p>Birmingham has two paid drop-off car parks. Both use cameras to read your number plate. Neither has a barrier. Both are linked to NCP, which handles payment.</p>
              <h3>Drop Off car park</h3>
              <ul>
                <li>Free for up to 10 minutes.</li>
                <li>£7 for 10 to 15 minutes.</li>
                <li>£8 for 15 to 20 minutes.</li>
                <li>Then £14, £20 and so on for each 5 minutes up to 30 minutes. After that the charge rises in steps.</li>
                <li>It's a 5 to 10 minute walk to the terminal. A free bus also runs.</li>
              </ul>
              <h3>Premium Set Down</h3>
              <ul>
                <li>£8 for the first 15 minutes. It's right outside the terminal.</li>
                <li>Blue Badge holders get the first 30 minutes free. They must have it validated at the NCP cabin, with the passenger present.</li>
              </ul>

              <h3>How you get a PCN</h3>
              <p>You don't pay within 24 hours of leaving.</p>

              <h3>Free alternative</h3>
              <p>Use the Drop Off car park. It's free for 10 minutes. You can still get a PCN (which you can still appeal) if you stay past the 10 minute mark.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="grounds-section sources-section">
              <h2>Sources</h2>
              <ul>
                <li>Birmingham Airport, <strong>Dropping off and picking up from BHX</strong>: <a href="https://www.birminghamairport.co.uk/parking/drop-off-and-pick-up/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.birminghamairport.co.uk/parking/drop-off-and-pick-up/</a></li>
                <li>Birmingham Airport, <strong>Drop Off Car Park prices</strong>: <a href="https://www.birminghamairport.co.uk/parking/drop-off-car-park/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.birminghamairport.co.uk/parking/drop-off-car-park/</a></li>
                <li>Birmingham Airport, <strong>Premium Set Down</strong>: <a href="https://www.birminghamairport.co.uk/parking/premium-set-down/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.birminghamairport.co.uk/parking/premium-set-down/</a></li>
                <li>Birmingham Airport, <strong>Byelaws</strong>: <a href="https://corporate.birminghamairport.co.uk/birmingham-airport-byelaws/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://corporate.birminghamairport.co.uk/birmingham-airport-byelaws/</a></li>
                <li>Protection of Freedoms Act 2012, <strong>Schedule 4</strong>: <a href="https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2012/9/schedule/4" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2012/9/schedule/4</a></li>
                <li>POPLA, <strong>Appeal guide</strong>: <a href="https://www.popla.co.uk/appeal-guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.popla.co.uk/appeal-guide</a></li>
                <li>GOV.UK, <strong>CCJs and your credit rating</strong>: <a href="https://www.gov.uk/county-court-judgments-ccj-for-debt/ccjs-and-your-credit-rating" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.gov.uk/county-court-judgments-ccj-for-debt/ccjs-and-your-credit-rating</a></li>
              </ul>
              <p>Birmingham's current Drop Off car park tariff is <strong>free for 10 minutes</strong>, then <strong>£7 for 10 to 15 minutes</strong>. Premium Set Down is currently <strong>£8 for the first 15 minutes</strong>.</p>
            </section>

            </div>

            <div class="disclaimer">
              <strong>Disclaimer:</strong> AppealAirportPCN.co.uk is a free information resource for UK drivers. Nothing on this site constitutes legal advice. Templates are provided as a starting point, always review your specific circumstances. For complex cases, consider consulting a solicitor or Citizens Advice.
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

</BaseLayout>
